filesToTouch.what:
The proof that the split is correct, exercised across TWO real prefixes in ONE process. Register two mounts via registerSetMount — 'live-animals' at '/live-animals' and 'plant-products' at '/plant-products' (a mount-table entry only; no plugin is registered) — then:
(1) inside withSetContext('live-animals'), assert pagePath/hubPath/createPath/dashboardPath/breadcrumbs return `/live-animals/notifications/J/slug`, `/live-animals/notifications/J`, `/live-animals/notifications`, `/live-animals` (NO trailing slash);
(2) inside withSetContext('plant-products'), assert the same builders return the `/plant-products/...` equivalents — SAME PROCESS, same module instance, different strings. This is acceptance point 4;
(3) assert the ROUTE-SHAPE builders are prefix-free under BOTH contexts — pageRoutePath('x') === '/notifications/{journeyId}/x', hubRoutePath() === '/notifications/{journeyId}', dashboardRoutePath() === '/' exactly, createRoutePath() === '/notifications' — because Hapi's routes.prefix supplies the mount and a doubled prefix is the failure mode this test exists to catch;
(4) assert dashboardPath() has NO `|| '/'` fallback behaviour: it returns the set base verbatim under each context;
(5) assert BASE is no longer exported (importing it yields undefined) so nothing can re-capture a prefix at module load.
